# WebGL with 1 Million Points

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Generating 1 million points takes a few seconds in Elixir. WebGL renders them
fluidly in the browser; SVG would freeze the page.

Note: Sending 1M floats over the Kino wire takes a moment — this is expected.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scattergl}

n = 1_000_000
x = for _ <- 1..n, do: :rand.uniform()
y = for _ <- 1..n, do: :rand.uniform()

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Scattergl.new(
    x: x,
    y: y,
    mode: "markers",
    marker: %{size: 1, color: "rgba(50, 100, 200, 0.3)"}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "WebGL with 1 Million Points")
|> Plotly.show()
```
